Written by hand for this repository on 2026-11-16 (the symbol editor's
design, section 10), no third-party content: every drawing here is our own,
named as KiCad names its kinds of part.
- symedit-small_parts.kicad_sym, the design's own symbols:
  - OPAMP2, a dual amplifier: units A (pins 1, 2, 3) and B (7, 6, 5) and a
    third unit holding the power pins (8 V+, 4 V-);
  - OPAMP2_ALT, derived from OPAMP2 (extends), its own value and description;
  - PWR3V3, a global power symbol (+3V3, one hidden power input);
  - CHECKME, four findings of KiCad's symbol checker on purpose: pin 3 twice
    in unit 1 (A and B), pin 2 0.254 mm (10 mil) off the 50 mil grid, pin 1 a
    hidden power input (VDD), and the designator prefix U1 ending in a digit.
- symedit-small.kicad_sch places OPAMP2's units A and B as U1 and a resistor
  as R1 (its drawing our own, its lib id Device:R), each with its copy in the
  sheet's lib_symbols; symedit-small.kicad_pro and sym-lib-table make
  symedit-small_parts the project's library.
- legacy.lib, one symbol in KiCad 5's legacy format (LEGACY_R).
- parts.lbr, one Eagle device set (EAGLE_R, the symbol RES).
The KiCad files carry no comment (their formats have none), so this file
holds their license.
